# CR 616.1: Words of Wisdom makes the AI draw a card while the AI's Thought
# Reflection ("draw two instead") and the human's Notion Thief ("the opponent
# skips that draw and you draw a card") both replace it. The affected player
# (the AI) chooses; candidates come in play order, so 0 is Notion Thief and 1
# is Thought Reflection.
# Thought Reflection first: the draw becomes two draws for the AI, each a new
# Draw event Thought Reflection cannot touch again (hasRun) but Notion Thief
# still can. Each is diverted: the human draws two instead, the AI none.
# Human library 5 - 2 (Words of Wisdom) - 2 (diverted) = 1.
queue replacement 1
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 2 U
tapformana human 3 U
queue paygeneric U
castspell human 1
resolvestack
